From e54acdb3afe13cb2bfad97b787861f0f0a2dd260 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 11:48:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] version: bump EXTENDNO to Reaper_v2.4.3

v2.4.2 images are already on the test ladder and have been run on the
RT-BE96U, so the security-audit remediation cannot ship under that string -
two different images would answer to one version. Same reason the v2.4.0
rebuild became v2.4.1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src-rt/version.conf | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/release/src-rt/version.conf b/release/src-rt/version.conf
index 910045c43c..3e38d3acbf 100644
--- a/release/src-rt/version.conf
+++ b/release/src-rt/version.conf
@@ -4,6 +4,6 @@ KERNEL_VER_AM=$(subst .,,$(KERNEL_VER))
 FS_VER_AM=$(subst .,,$(FS_VER))
 
 SERIALNO=102.8
-EXTENDNO=Reaper_v2.4.2
+EXTENDNO=Reaper_v2.4.3
 
 RCNO=0
-- 
2.25.1

